  "notes": [
    "Haarlemmerweg 217-283 (pand 0363100012101656, built 1998), the north wall block of the GWL-terrein, 90 m along the Haarlemmerweg facing the Westerpark across the Haarlemmervaart; 26 m, nine storeys.",
    "walls[0] the Haarlemmerweg front (panels 18, 12, 13, 8, 7 and the 2.5 m entrance notches 15, 17, 10, 33, the tall east end 59 and 1; crops w02-0, w05-360, w04-360, w06-360L, w07-0, 2021-03-24/22, square on and leaf-off): red-brown brick, small white-framed windows about 0.75 x 1.4 m on a 1.2 m pitch with blind bays scattered differently on every storey (openBays, read off w02-0 and w05-360), a taller ground storey (storeyFactors 1.35). The signature: an enclosed access gallery, a dark-framed glass band on a pale concrete deck hung on struts, cantilevered about 1.8 m from the fifth storey up into the sixth along the whole front (kit windowBox with spread, frame and deck, issue #65); on the west panel it stops three quarters along (bays 0-14 of 20). A row of short windows sits over the band on the sixth storey (storeyShapes).",
    "walls[1] the east end (panel 48, crop w03-77 2021-12-30): the same brick and windows without the gallery, scattered on alternating storeys.",
    "walls[2] the courtyard front (panel 22, crop w01-180 2019-11-08, 43 % foliage): concrete-framed balcony galleries on every upper storey; drawn as brick with pale bar balconies. Not seen from the park.",
    "INFERRED: the roof-level step walls and the west party wall (otherWalls brick grid).",
    "Measured 2026-10-25 (measure.ts, evidence in measured.json): groups 0, 1 take the photo's wall and glass colour, window shape, bay count and front class; walls[1] bays 3 from the likeness grid (padded measurement 4)."
  ],
